From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: find a station that has been answered but not yet acked

An MLD station could associate, report every link up, and never move a byte.
The AP had no 4-address peer interface for it, the station had no idea, and
nothing ever retried. Measured twice on hardware 2026-07-29: once on a cold
boot where two agents associated at the same moment, and once - reproducibly -
by removing and re-adding a link with SETUP_LINK_RECONFIG.

The 4-address peer is created either from handle_assoc_cb(), or lazily from
ieee802_11_rx_from_unknown() when the first 4-address frame arrives. That
second path exists precisely because the frame can arrive before the
association is complete, and it is careful about it: a station that is only
WLAN_STA_ASSOC_REQ_OK gets pending_wds_enable set instead of an immediate
enable, and handle_assoc_cb() acts on that flag once the association lands.

None of that care is reached for an MLD station, because ap_get_sta() does not
return one in that window - its MLD fallback requires WLAN_STA_ASSOC, which is
set later, after the Association Response TX status. So the frame looks like it
came from an unknown station and is answered with a deauth, which the station
discards because it is unprotected and PMF is on.

The station therefore stays associated while the AP never enables WDS for it,
and it never gets a second chance: mac80211 reports an unexpected 4-address
frame exactly once per station (WLAN_STA_4ADDR_EVENT is set and never cleared),
so every later frame is dropped in silence.

Only the lookup is missing, so add only the lookup, and keep it local to this
caller: a station that is WLAN_STA_ASSOC_REQ_OK and not yet WLAN_STA_ASSOC,
which is exactly what ap_get_sta() cannot see.

Widening ap_get_sta() itself is emphatically not the same change, and was tried
first: its MLD fallback also matches on setup_link_addr, so it can return a
different sta_info than a caller expects. Every agent then failed its 4-way
handshake with reason 15 and the mesh stayed down until the build was reverted.

Deterministic reproducer on an agent:
  wpa_cli -i bsta-mld-3 setup_link_reconfig delete=1
  wpa_cli -i bsta-mld-3 setup_link_reconfig add=1
  -> peer netdev ap-mld-2.staN disappears, node unreachable, links still shown

Signed-off-by: WOZIWRT <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
diff -urN a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c
--- a/src/ap/ieee802_11.c	2026-07-29 17:56:13.544998748 +0200
+++ b/src/ap/ieee802_11.c	2026-07-29 17:56:13.545683632 +0200
@@ -8171,6 +8171,64 @@
 }
 
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+/* Find an MLD station that has been answered but not yet acked.
+ *
+ * ap_get_sta() will not: its MLD fallback requires WLAN_STA_ASSOC, which is set
+ * only in handle_assoc_cb(), after the TX status for the Association Response.
+ * A 4-address frame that arrives inside that window therefore looks like it
+ * came from an unknown station and is answered with a deauth - which the
+ * station discards, because it is unprotected and PMF is on.
+ *
+ * The station stays associated while the AP never enables WDS for it, and there
+ * is no second chance: mac80211 reports an unexpected 4-address frame exactly
+ * once per station and never clears that flag. Measured twice on hardware
+ * 2026-07-29, once on a cold boot with two agents associating at the same
+ * moment and once reproducibly via SETUP_LINK_RECONFIG.
+ *
+ * The caller already knows how to handle this state - it sets
+ * pending_wds_enable rather than enabling WDS immediately, and handle_assoc_cb()
+ * acts on it once the association completes. All that is missing is finding the
+ * station. Keep that search here, narrow: only a station that is
+ * WLAN_STA_ASSOC_REQ_OK and not yet WLAN_STA_ASSOC, which is exactly the window
+ * ap_get_sta() cannot see. Widening ap_get_sta() itself is not the same change -
+ * its MLD fallback also matches on setup_link_addr, so it can return a
+ * different sta_info than the caller expects, and doing that broke the 4-way
+ * handshake for every agent when tried.
+ */
+static struct sta_info * hostapd_ml_get_sta_pending_assoc(
+	struct hostapd_data *hapd, const u8 *src)
+{
+	u8 link_id;
+
+	if (!hapd->conf->mld_ap)
+		return NULL;
+
+	for (link_id = 0; link_id < MAX_NUM_MLD_LINKS; link_id++) {
+		struct hostapd_data *h = hostapd_mld_get_link_bss(hapd, link_id);
+		struct sta_info *s;
+
+		if (!h)
+			continue;
+
+		for (s = h->sta_list; s; s = s->next) {
+			if (!s->mld_info.mld_sta)
+				continue;
+			if (s->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC)
+				continue;
+			if (!(s->flags & WLAN_STA_ASSOC_REQ_OK))
+				continue;
+			if (!os_memcmp(s->setup_link_addr, src, ETH_ALEN) ||
+			    !os_memcmp(s->addr, src, ETH_ALEN))
+				return s;
+		}
+	}
+
+	return NULL;
+}
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
+
+
 void ieee802_11_rx_from_unknown(struct hostapd_data *hapd, const u8 *src,
 				int wds)
 {
@@ -8179,6 +8237,8 @@
 	sta = ap_get_sta(hapd, src);
 
 #ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	if (!sta)
+		sta = hostapd_ml_get_sta_pending_assoc(hapd, src);
 	if (sta && sta->mld_info.mld_sta)
 		sta = sta->mld_assoc_sta;
 #endif
